From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ppe: avoid fortify false positive on encap free

  ppe_drv_tun_encap_free() recovers the instance with container_of() from
  its kref and then clears the whole structure.  Under 6.12's
  FORTIFY_SOURCE the dynamic object size of that recovered pointer is
  still the 4-byte kref member, so the clear is reported as a field
  overflow (-Werror=attribute-warning) and the build fails.  The clear
  covers exactly sizeof(*ptec), so hide the pointer from the optimizer
  instead of changing the code.

diff -ruN a/drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_encap.c b/drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_encap.c
--- a/drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_encap.c
+++ b/drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_encap.c
@@ -556,6 +556,13 @@
 		ppe_drv_warn("%p: encap entry delete failed for tunnel index %u", ptec, ptec->tun_idx);
 		return;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * FORTIFY_SOURCE's dynamic object size tracking keeps the 4-byte
+	 * kref subobject for a pointer recovered with container_of(), so
+	 * clearing the whole instance looks like a field overflow.  Hide the
+	 * recovered pointer from the optimizer; the clear itself is exact.
+	 */
+	OPTIMIZER_HIDE_VAR(ptec);
 	memset(ptec, 0, sizeof(*ptec));
 }
 
